---
import { person } from '../data/resume';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const { '@context': context, ...profile } = person;
---

<Base title="About" description="About me" schema={{ '@context': context, '@type': 'ProfilePage', mainEntity: profile }}>
	<header class="page-head">
		<h1 data-decode>About</h1>
		<p>Me, me and more me.</p>
	</header>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			I work in systems and security and mostly black-box testing of web apps and any other rabbit hole which excites me. I am most interested in small business logic flaws.
		</p>
		<p>
			Speaking of bounties, I've found a couple of bugs in live engagements (<a href="https://bugcrowd.com/h/thev123">Bugcrowd</a>) but still yearn for an <em>original</em>, <em>vetted</em> P<5 finding soon :<
		</p>
		<p>
			I also build software. Recent projects include an Android safety app, a private chat over TCP using
			post-quantum cryptography, and a health assistant for university students (the last ones kinda mid).
		</p>
		<p>
			This site collects <a href="/writeups/">writeups</a> of security work, shorter <a href="/notes/">notes</a>, and <a href="/projects/">projects</a>. If you are here to hire me, start with the <a href="/resume/">resume</a>. The hardware and tools I work with are on <a href="/uses/">uses</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Find me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/avishekwithav/">LinkedIn</a> or
			<a href="https://github.com/notDeadCaller">GitHub</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 id="colophon">Colophon</h2>
		<p>
			Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and hosted on GitHub Pages. The visual language draws on the interfaces of Watch Dogs and
			Cyberpunk 2077. type shi.
		</p>
		<blockquote>{SITE.quote}</blockquote>
	</div>
</Base>
